{
  "_comment": [
    "Tier-3 (the wash tier) constants, from src/detector_t3.py's defaults.",
    "",
    "enabled_default is false because the calibration failed: the statistic",
    "saturates at its cap on the real rotor and on insects, HVAC fans, tracked",
    "vehicles and helicopters alike, so it does not separate them. The smallest",
    "weighted false-alarm increment reachable at any threshold on the 2.03 h",
    "negative corpus was 4.87/h against an allowance of 0.40.",
    "",
    "It is kept, built, tested and ported because on the first real propeller",
    "recordings it was the only tier that detected anything: v1 peaks at 1.76",
    "against a 1.70 threshold and raises zero events, Tier-2 raises zero, and",
    "Tier-3 latches 94% of the 4 m capture and 88% of the 10 m one. The signal",
    "is there; what is missing is a way to tell it from a fan. Whether the tier",
    "runs on a unit is a firmware setting."
  ],
